From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:15:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PM / devfreq: passive: do not wait for the policies of
 offline CPUs

The passive governor's registration wants a cpufreq policy for every
possible CPU that has OPPs, and defers the probe until each exists. A CPU
that is offline has no policy, so a system that keeps CPUs offline until
later never gets past the deferral.

On the MT6797 Gemini PDA the two Cortex-A72 cores come up late from a
module, or not at all, and now have OPP tables. With them offline,
mtk-cci-devfreq deferred on every retry. Each retry raised the CPU rail to
the CCI's top voltage and dropped the request again, leaving the CCI at
its boot rate with the rail at the A53 policies' request. The station then
stopped responding until the watchdog reset it.

Leave offline CPUs without a policy out of the registration. Once they
come up, a policy created for them is skipped as one the governor has no
parent data for, and a CPU that cpufreq left out and so has no policy at
all is now skipped too, instead of failing every update with -EINVAL and
holding the CCI at its last rate.
---
 drivers/devfreq/governor_passive.c | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/devfreq/governor_passive.c b/drivers/devfreq/governor_passive.c
index 67936b217..6c9c99360 100644
--- a/drivers/devfreq/governor_passive.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/governor_passive.c
@@ -125,12 +125,14 @@ static int get_target_freq_with_cpufreq(struct devfreq *devfreq,
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	for_each_online_cpu(cpu) {
+		/*
+		 * A CPU without a policy is not followed: it has no OPPs, its
+		 * policy is not created yet, or it came up after cpufreq
+		 * left it out.
+		 */
 		policy = cpufreq_cpu_get(cpu);
-		if (!policy) {
-			if (!cpu_without_opps(cpu))
-				ret = -EINVAL;
+		if (!policy)
 			continue;
-		}
 
 		parent_cpu_data = get_parent_cpu_data(p_data, policy);
 		if (!parent_cpu_data) {
@@ -314,7 +316,12 @@ static int cpufreq_passive_register_notifier(struct devfreq *devfreq)
 	for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) {
 		policy = cpufreq_cpu_get(cpu);
 		if (!policy) {
-			if (cpu_without_opps(cpu))
+			/*
+			 * A CPU without OPPs is never a parent. An offline CPU
+			 * may have no policy until it comes up, and a policy
+			 * created later is left out like any unknown one.
+			 */
+			if (cpu_without_opps(cpu) || !cpu_online(cpu))
 				continue;
 			ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
 			goto err;
-- 
